Course Content:
The development of Christian theology in the modern context will be highlighted by discussing various theological positions. We will focus on the 19th and 20th centuries, starting with Schleiermacher and ending up with recent theological trends as postliberal theology, the theological interpretation of Scripture and the New Perspective on Paul.

